WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.500
So how do you feel now?

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.180
Like, through all this, throughout this process, how do you feel at this moment, right now? [background noise of river barge traffic]

3
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.940
I feel great, because I’ve learned so much.

4
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:17.680
Not about just my family, but I have traced families that I’m not related to.

5
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.240
And I know that a baby died in childbirth.

6
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.840
You know, it’s one of those . . . it feels good when I know that certain . . . I know some people died from suicide.

7
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.160
I know cholera was bad.

8
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.760
They had malaria out here.

9
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.520
You know, it’s one of those things I didn’t know, like they were teaching slaves how to read.

10
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.500
All my life I kept hearing that slaves were not allowed to learn how to read.

11
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.040
So, some places they built schools.

12
00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.160
They gave them ceremonies.

13
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.760
They let them do certain things, which goes against those, the movies that I watched.

14
00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:45.920
So, I feel great.

15
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.100
I hope other people will go out and look and help a friend or whatever with your ancestors.

16
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.620
Like I tell people, it doesn’t have to be your family.

17
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.960
You can just sit on a census record, pick a name, and try to find that person.
